{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Resume-to-form fixture for the Smart Paste extractor experiment (workplan Chunk 1). Each case pairs a free-text source with a form; every field has a ground-truth expectation. People, companies and contacts are fictional; emails use the reserved .example domain and phone numbers use invalid or reserved ranges.",
  "matchModes": {
    "exact": "case-insensitive equality after collapsing whitespace",
    "digits": "the last 10 digits of the fill equal the last 10 digits of the value",
    "url": "same host and path, ignoring scheme, leading www. and a trailing slash",
    "month": "the fill names this year and month (value is YYYY-MM)",
    "set": "the fill lists every item, comma- or semicolon-separated, in any order",
    "contains": "the fill contains this phrase, case-insensitive",
    "empty": "the field must stay empty: the source does not state it, or it is a secure field",
    "skip": "not scored: the value is derivable only relative to today's date"
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "r1-bio",
      "kind": "first-person bio",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Ananya Iyer, a senior iOS engineer with 9 years of experience. Since March 2021 I have led the patient-app team at Lumora Health in Bengaluru. Before that I spent four years at Kestrel Payments building their merchant SDK in Swift and Objective-C. Day to day I work in Swift, SwiftUI, Combine and Core Data, and I mentor two junior developers. I studied Computer Science (B.Tech) at the College of Engineering, Pune, graduating in 2016. You can reach me at ananya.iyer@lumora.example or +91 55555 01234. Portfolio: https://ananya.example.dev, LinkedIn: linkedin.com/in/ananya-iyer-ios. Address: Flat 4B, Palm Grove Apartments, 12th Main Road, Indiranagar, Bengaluru 560038, Karnataka."
    },
    {
      "id": "r2-resume",
      "kind": "bullet resume",
      "text": "MARCUS DELACROIX-OYELARAN\nData Engineer · Austin, TX\nmarcus.d.oyelaran@mailbox.example | (512) 555-0147 | github.com/mdoyelaran | linkedin.com/in/marcus-oyelaran\n\nEXPERIENCE\nSenior Data Engineer, Brightwater Analytics, Austin, TX    Jun 2022 – Present\n• Built streaming pipelines in Python, Apache Kafka and Spark processing 2B events/day\n• Cut warehouse cost 38% by moving batch jobs to dbt on Snowflake\nData Engineer, Harlow Freight, Dallas, TX    Aug 2019 – May 2022\n• Owned Airflow orchestration for 140 DAGs\n\nEDUCATION\nM.S. Computer Science, University of Texas at Austin, 2019\nB.S. Mathematics, Rice University, 2017\n\nSKILLS\nPython, SQL, Apache Kafka, Spark, dbt, Snowflake, Airflow, Terraform"
    },
    {
      "id": "r3-cv",
      "kind": "European CV, dd/mm dates",
      "text": "Lebenslauf / CV\nName: Sofie Brandt-Halvorsen\nPosition sought: Product Designer\nE-mail: sofie.brandt@studio-nord.example\nTelefon: +49 30 0000 1290\nAnschrift: Lindenstraße 42, 10969 Berlin, Germany\nPortfolio: https://sofiebrandt.example\n\nExperience\n01/04/2020 – present: Lead Product Designer, Studio Nord GmbH, Berlin\n15/09/2016 – 31/03/2020: UX Designer, Kaskade Mobility, Hamburg\n\nEducation: MA Interaction Design, Universität der Künste Berlin (2016)\nTools: Figma, Framer, Principle, Adobe Illustrator\nLanguages: German (native), Norwegian (native), English (C2)"
    },
    {
      "id": "r4-message",
      "kind": "email message",
      "text": "Thanks for the call today! As promised, my details for the speaker form:\n\nKenji Watanabe-Morales, Staff ML Engineer, Orbitra AI (Tokyo office)\nTalk: \"Distilling small on-device models\" (we agreed on the 30-minute slot)\nkenji.wm@orbitra.example · +81 3-5555-0198 · https://github.com/kwatanabe-m\nBio: I build on-device inference for Orbitra's camera app; before Orbitra I spent 5 years at Sora Robotics.\nX: @kenji_wm\n\nBest,\nKenji"
    }
  ],
